  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>The particle is moving in a horizontal circle, so it is accelerated towards the centre with magnitude&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msup><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>r</mi></mfrac></math>.&nbsp;The horizontal force on the particle is due to the spring and is given by&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>k</mi><mi>x</mi></math>,&nbsp;where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math>&nbsp;is the elongation and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>k</mi></math> is the spring constant.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>k</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>m</mi><msup><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mi>r</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi><msup><mi>&#969;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi><msup><mi>&#969;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>l</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>m</mi><msup><mi>&#969;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfenced><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi><msup><mi>&#969;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msub><mi>l</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>m</mi><msup><mi>&#969;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msub><mi>l</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>m</mi><msup><mi>&#969;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></math></p>",
